1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,347
Business Case 08 begins when a versioned assessment or screening task is
assigned at an authorized stage.

2
00:00:08,347 --> 00:00:13,256
A correctable, human-reviewed outcome preserves notice, response windows
and redress.

3
00:00:13,256 --> 00:00:15,711
The governed record is CTK-004.

4
00:00:15,711 --> 00:00:20,621
The accountable actors are Candidate, Recruiter, Screening Reviewer,
Candidate Support.

5
00:00:20,621 --> 00:00:27,985
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:27,985 --> 00:00:32,583
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:32,583 --> 00:00:40,859
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:40,859 --> 00:00:45,457
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:45,457 --> 00:00:48,419
Process 1, Candidate: Review notice and consent.

10
00:00:48,419 --> 00:00:54,765
The action acknowledge current notice produces notice and consent
receipt in the Regulated case ledger.

11
00:00:54,765 --> 00:00:57,727
Process 2, Screening Coordinator: Prepare provider request.

12
00:00:57,727 --> 00:01:05,343
The action validate minimum data and send preview produces prepared
request and correlation key in the Integration ledger.

13
00:01:05,343 --> 00:01:07,882
Process 3, Candidate: Correct or dispute.

14
00:01:07,882 --> 00:01:14,229
The action submit protected response produces dispute and decision pause
in the Regulated case ledger.

15
00:01:14,229 --> 00:01:17,191
Process 4, Screening Reviewer: Record governed outcome.

16
00:01:17,191 --> 00:01:23,538
The action review separated evidence produces human outcome and
candidate-safe status in the Outcome ledger.

17
00:01:23,538 --> 00:01:26,470
The actual product route is /hr/cases/CASE-DEMO-001.

18
00:01:26,470 --> 00:01:33,311
It presents regulated screening and adverse-action timeline in the
surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:33,311 --> 00:01:45,528
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:45,528 --> 00:01:48,449
The seeded workbench follows record CASE-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:48,449 --> 00:02:05,002
Its governed fields are Notice version, BG-US-CA-v5 , acknowledged;
Provider status, Report returned , review required; Response clock, 3
business days remaining; Dispute, Identity mismatch , open; Decision
effect, Paused; Reviewer, Screening Ops West.

22
00:02:05,002 --> 00:02:14,252
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

23
00:02:14,252 --> 00:02:18,309
With Screening Reviewer selected, we perform record governed human
outcome.

24
00:02:18,309 --> 00:02:23,582
The guard requires notice, consent, response clock, dispute and evidence
separation all pass.

25
00:02:23,582 --> 00:02:35,346
The state changes from Decision paused to Cleared after human review,
records ScreeningOutcomeRecorded, writes to the Regulated case ledger,
and creates the handoff: Decision owner receives minimum outcome only.

26
00:02:35,346 --> 00:02:39,408
We now exercise the controlled exception: Open candidate dispute.

27
00:02:39,408 --> 00:02:44,823
The prepared failure is Candidate disputes an identity mismatch during
protected window.

28
00:02:44,823 --> 00:02:54,301
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

29
00:02:54,301 --> 00:02:57,733
The owned recovery is Resolve dispute and resume.

30
00:02:57,733 --> 00:03:02,024
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

31
00:03:02,024 --> 00:03:07,601
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

32
00:03:07,601 --> 00:03:16,611
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through response-window compliance and correction turnaround and
minimum-context next-actor work.

33
00:03:16,611 --> 00:03:19,214
Business Case 08 is complete.

34
00:03:19,214 --> 00:03:34,313
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

35
00:03:34,313 --> 00:03:39,519
A correctable, human-reviewed outcome preserves notice, response windows
and redress.

36
00:03:39,519 --> 00:03:45,246
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
